From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANYBOOK: GKI: x86: anybook_amd: add the symbols NVIDIA's open
 modules need

NVIDIA's open kernel modules (open-gpu-kernel-modules 615.78.08: nvidia.ko, nvidia-modeset.ko and
nvidia-drm.ko) are built as AnyBook vendor modules for the G14's RTX 5070 Ti Laptop GPU (GB205), as the
alternative to nouveau that NVK on NVIDIA's driver runs on (ANAL-297). Vendor modules are unsigned, so
under MODULE_SIG_PROTECT they may only use symbols on the KMI list, and the trimmed GKI exports nothing
else. With their Tegra SoC and coherent-memory (NUMA hotplug) code compiled out on x86_64, the three
modules need 61 symbols that are on none of the x86_64 lists yet:

  address_space_init_once close_fd console_lock console_unlock cpufreq_get dev_printk_emit dma_iova_free dma_iova_try_alloc drm_atomic_get_colorop_state drm_atomic_set_colorop_for_plane drm_atomic_set_crtc_for_connector drm_atomic_set_crtc_for_plane drm_atomic_set_mode_prop_for_crtc drm_colorop_cleanup drm_edid_override_connector_update drm_file_get_master drm_gem_mmap_obj drm_gem_prime_fd_to_handle drm_master_put drm_mode_create drm_property_create_bool drm_property_lookup_blob drm_property_replace_global_blob drm_vma_node_is_allowed drm_vma_offset_lookup_locked fget filp_close filp_open follow_pfnmap_end follow_pfnmap_start get_task_pid init_pid_ns iterate_fd jiffies_to_timespec64 kernel_read kernel_write mod_node_page_state pcibios_resource_to_bus pcie_reset_flr pci_find_host_bridge percpu_counter_add_batch percpu_counter_batch pid_vnr pin_user_pages proc_create_data proc_mkdir_mode proc_remove put_pid screen_info seq_read_iter set_page_dirty_lock shmem_kernel_file_setup strncat task_active_pid_ns vfs_fallocate vga_set_legacy_decoding __vmalloc_noprof vmf_insert_mixed vprintk wait_for_device_probe wait_for_random_bytes

Eight of them (fget filp_close kernel_read kernel_write pid_vnr proc_remove put_pid __vmalloc_noprof)
were already exported for GKI modules but protected from unsigned ones. filp_open and close_fd stay in
the ANDROID_GKI_VFS namespace, which the modules import explicitly: NVIDIA's runtime D3 keeps the GPU's
PCI sysfs config file open.

No existing entry is removed or moved, so every existing export keeps its CRC.

Change-Id: I6d5819774cd41e2f72202918235d67d135604fd7
